        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "CORRECTION: this upload is the stage-1 loader only. I trimmed the file to the end of its PE image, assuming the overlay was junk padding. Per Thereallo's analysis of the same campaign (thereallo.dev, South Park S29E03 lure, Oct 2026), the overlay also carries a ChaCha20-encrypted second stage, and the file ends in a 64-byte footer (key^mask, nonce, sizes ^ fnv1a(mask)) that the loader reads from its own file. Both were cut off here, so this sample cannot reach stage 2 on its own, which likely explains the clean sandbox verdicts. Stage 2 is the stealer that uses the YouTube channel UC18vFC1xgebddr_7NsvgBYA and gist jasonterra69 dead drops (XOR key ZhxchsdfhSGdfgsgdfAJsakdaksdk2364236AH; my earlier comments/ThreatFox entry quoted only its first 27 chars) and C2 beenetprotect.com/lgz/gdata. The full original was not kept. Same builder as 58dffd262bb9b3c815f1017735cfa214fbbb029af8bd4cbba42c3d8db218e582 (identical imphash and Rich header)."
      }
